# Typing ":" and part of a name in a comment box offers GitHub's emoji, as github.com does:
# ↩ puts the first one's character in place of what was typed, ↓ moves down the list, and
# Esc closes the list and leaves the comment open with what was typed. The list is a window
# of AppKit's own, so it's what lands in the box that's checked.
wait settled
open tamarinworks/atrium#2928
wait settled
click image #doc
wait settled
scroll scroll 2 down 300
hover textarea
click button "Add a comment"
wait until text "Comment on line 22"

type ":ta"
wait until textarea 2 has value ":ta"
press return
wait until textarea 2 has value "🌮"

type " :ta"
press down return
wait until textarea 2 has value "🌮 🎉"

type " :ship"
press esc
wait until textarea 2 has value "🌮 🎉 :ship"
wait until text "Comment on line 22"
